STUDENT PROJECT CATALOG PORTAL

DATA MODELS AND DATABASE STRUCTURE

4. DATA MODELS

The database is a set of collections, where each document describes one real-world thing.

The portal has five core collections and two stretch collections.

4.1 COLLECTION OVERVIEW

1. User
   What it stores: Students and admins.
   Related stories: S1-S5, S29, S34, A1, A21.

2. Project
   What it stores: Official and community projects.
   Related stories: S6-S14, S21-S28, A3-A13.

3. Request
   What it stores: A student's ask for a project and its status.
   Related stories: S15-S20, A16-A20.

4. Review
   What it stores: Rating and comment after download.
   Related stories: S35-S36, A23.

5. Report
   What it stores: Flag for rule-breaking content.
   Related stories: S37, A14.

6. Wishlist (Stretch)
   What it stores: Saved projects.
   Related stories: S38.

7. Message (Stretch)
   What it stores: Request chat.
   Related stories: S39, A25.


4.2 RELATIONSHIPS

The database relationships are as follows:

1. A User creates many Projects.
2. A User makes many Requests, and a Project receives many Requests.
3. A User writes many Reviews, and a Project has many Reviews.
4. A User files many Reports.


4.3 USER COLLECTION

The User collection stores student and administrator account information.

Fields:

1. name
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Display name.

2. email
   Type: String
   Required: Yes, Unique
   Meaning: Login ID, stored lowercase.

3. passwordHash
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: bcrypt hash, never the real password.

4. role
   Type: student / admin
   Required: Yes (Default: student)
   Meaning: Controls permissions.

5. bio
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Short intro for author profile.

6. avatarUrl
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Profile picture.

7. postingStatus
   Type: active / warned / banned
   Required: Yes (Default: active)
   Meaning: Whether the user can post projects.

8. warningCount
   Type: Number
   Required: Yes (Default: 0)
   Meaning: Rule violations so far.

9. resetTokenHash
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Hashed forgot-password token.

10. resetTokenExpires
    Type: Date
    Required: No
    Meaning: Token expiry time.

11. createdAt, updatedAt
    Type: Date
    Required: Auto
    Meaning: Join date for the admin user list.

USER COLLECTION RULES

1. Never return passwordHash or reset fields in API responses.
2. A banned user can still browse and request but cannot submit projects.


4.4 PROJECT COLLECTION

One model holds both official and community projects, separated by source.

BASIC DETAILS

1. title
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Project name.

2. slug
   Type: String
   Required: Yes, Unique
   Meaning: URL-friendly name.

3. course
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Example: CSE, IT, MCA.

4. techStack
   Type: [String]
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Example: React, Node, MongoDB.

5. level
   Type: beginner / intermediate / advanced
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Difficulty.

6. description
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: What the project does.

7. whatInclude
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Example: source code, report, DB script.

8. howToRun
   Type: String
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Setup steps.


FILES

9. images
   Type: [{ url, publicId }]
   Required: Yes (Minimum 1)
   Meaning: Screenshots.

10. file
    Type: { publicId, sizeBytes, originalName }
    Required: Yes
    Meaning: The ZIP. Stores the private storage ID, not a public link, so downloads can be gated and expire.


OWNERSHIP AND SOURCE

11. source
    Type: official / community
    Required: Yes
    Meaning: Drives the badge.

12. createdBy
    Type: ObjectId → User
    Required: Yes
    Meaning: Who posted it.

13. termsAcceptedAt
    Type: Date
    Required: Community only
    Meaning: Proof the author accepted the rules.


REVIEW WORKFLOW

14. submissionStatus
    Type: draft / pending_review / changes_requested / approved / rejected
    Required: Yes
    Meaning: Position in the approval flow.

15. reviewNote
    Type: String
    Required: On reject or changes
    Meaning: Admin feedback.

16. reviewedBy
    Type: ObjectId → User
    Required: No
    Meaning: Deciding admin.

17. reviewedAt
    Type: Date
    Required: No
    Meaning: Decision time.

18. isActive
    Type: Boolean (Default: true)
    Required: Yes
    Meaning: Soft delete or unpublish.


STATISTICS (MAINTAINED BY THE SERVER)

19. ratingAvg
    Type: Number (0-5)
    Meaning: Shown on the card.

20. ratingCount
    Type: Number
    Meaning: Number of reviews.

21. requestCount
    Type: Number
    Meaning: Shown to the author.

22. downloadCount
    Type: Number
    Meaning: Shown to the author.

23. createdAt, updatedAt
    Type: Date
    Meaning: Used for the "newest" sort.


PROJECT STATUS FLOW

Community status flow:

draft → pending_review → approved (live)

Other possible transitions:

pending_review → changes_requested

changes_requested → pending_review (after student edits and resubmits)

pending_review → rejected

Official projects created by an admin skip this workflow and start as approved.


PROJECT COLLECTION RULES

1. Publicly visible only if submissionStatus = approved and isActive = true.

2. Editing a live community project's content sets it back to pending_review.

3. Deleting means setting isActive = false. Documents are never removed, so past requests keep working.

4. A student can edit only projects where createdBy is their own ID.


4.5 REQUEST COLLECTION

The Request collection stores a student's project request and its approval status.

FIELDS

1. userId
   Type: ObjectId → User
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Who is asking.

2. projectId
   Type: ObjectId → Project
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: What they want.

3. note
   Type: String (Maximum about 300 characters)
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Why they need it.

4. status
   Type: pending / approved / rejected / delivered
   Required: Yes (Default: pending)
   Meaning: Current state.

5. adminReason
   Type: String
   Required: If rejected
   Meaning: Why it was rejected.

6. decidedBy
   Type: ObjectId → User
   Required: No
   Meaning: Admin (or author, if delegated).

7. decidedAt
   Type: Date
   Required: No
   Meaning: Decision time.

8. deliveredAt
   Type: Date
   Required: No
   Meaning: First successful download.

9. downloadCount
   Type: Number (Default: 0)
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Times downloaded.

10. createdAt, updatedAt
    Type: Date
    Required: Auto
    Meaning: Request date.


REQUEST STATUS FLOW

pending → approved → delivered

Or:

pending → rejected


REQUEST COLLECTION RULES

1. No duplicates: A user cannot hold two active (pending or approved) requests for the same project.

2. No self-requests: userId cannot equal the project's createdBy.

3. Download gate: The API allows download only when status is approved or delivered, and generates a short-lived link each time. The link itself is never stored.

4. Every status change triggers an email.


4.6 REVIEW COLLECTION

The Review collection stores project ratings and comments submitted by students after downloading a project.

FIELDS

1. userId
   Type: ObjectId → User
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Reviewer.

2. projectId
   Type: ObjectId → Project
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Reviewed project.

3. rating
   Type: Number (1-5)
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Stars.

4. comment
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Written feedback.

5. isHidden
   Type: Boolean (Default: false)
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Admin moderation.

6. createdAt, updatedAt
   Type: Date
   Required: Auto


REVIEW COLLECTION RULES

1. One review per user per project (unique on userId + projectId).

2. A review is allowed only if the user has a delivered request for the project and is not its author.

3. After any create, edit, delete or hide operation, recalculate the project's ratingAvg and ratingCount.


4.7 REPORT COLLECTION

The Report collection stores flags submitted for rule-breaking content.

FIELDS

1. reporterId
   Type: ObjectId → User
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Who reported.

2. targetType
   Type: project / review
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: What is reported.

3. targetId
   Type: ObjectId
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: ID of the project or review.

4. reason
   Type: plagiarism / malware / inappropriate / personal_data / other
   Required: Yes
   Meaning: Category.

5. details
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Extra explanation.

6. status
   Type: open / resolved / dismissed
   Required: Yes (Default: open)
   Meaning: Admin handling.

7. resolvedBy
   Type: ObjectId → User
   Required: No
   Meaning: Handling admin.

8. resolutionNote
   Type: String
   Required: No
   Meaning: Action taken.

9. createdAt
   Type: Date
   Required: Auto


4.8 STRETCH MODELS

WISHLIST

Fields:

1. userId → User
2. projectId → Project
3. createdAt

Constraint:

Unique on userId + projectId.


MESSAGE

Fields:

1. requestId → Request
2. senderId → User
3. text
4. createdAt


4.9 DATABASE INDEXES

The following indexes are defined to improve query performance and enforce uniqueness.

1. User Collection

   Index: email (unique)
   Purpose: Fast, unique login.

2. Project Collection

   Index: slug (unique)
   Purpose: Detail page by URL.

3. Project Collection

   Index: submissionStatus + isActive + source
   Purpose: Public listing and filters.

4. Project Collection

   Index: Text index on title, description, techStack.
   Purpose: Keyword search.

5. Project Collection

   Index: createdBy
   Purpose: My submissions and author profile.

6. Request Collection

   Index: userId + projectId
   Purpose: Duplicate check and My Requests.

7. Request Collection

   Index: status
   Purpose: Admin status filter.

8. Review Collection

   Index: userId + projectId (unique)
   Purpose: One review per project.

9. Review Collection

   Index: projectId
   Purpose: Reviews on the detail page.


